# Frontend Services & Types

## Service file pattern

Follow `src/services/authApi.ts`:

```typescript
import Configs from "@/configurations/appConfig";
import apiClient from "./apiClient";
import type { SomeRequest } from "@/types/request.types";
import type { SomeResponse, APIResponse } from "@/types/response.types";

const API_PATH = Configs.API_ENDPOINT + "/api/v1/...";

export const someApi = (request: SomeRequest) => {
  return apiClient.post<APIResponse<SomeResponse>>(API_PATH, request);
};
```

- Always use `apiClient` (HttpOnly cookie auth, refresh on 410)
- Base URL: `Configs.API_ENDPOINT` (default `http://localhost:8081`)
- Export named functions; group by domain (`jobApi.ts`, `companyApi.ts`, …)

## Response shape

```typescript
interface APIResponse<T> {
  code: number;      // backend success code: 1000
  message: string;
  result: T;
}

interface PageResponse<T> {
  data: T[];
  page: number;
  size: number;
  totalElements: number;
  totalPages: number;
}
```

- Paginated lists: `response.data.result.data`, totals from `totalElements`
- Request types: `src/types/request.types.ts`
- Response types: `src/types/response.types.ts`
- Enums synced from backend: `src/types/common.types.ts`
